.DS_Store
target/
node_modules/
.env
.env.*

# `/plan`, not `plan/`. In the three development worktrees `plan` is a *symlink*
# to the shared plan repository, and a pattern ending in `/` matches directories
# only — so `plan/` left the symlink untracked-but-committable and `git add -A`
# would have put it on a code branch. DEV-PROTOCOL §9 forbids exactly that.
/plan

# Python bytecode from the differential reference. `reference/` is source that two
# implementations are diffed against; a .pyc in a commit is noise at best and, in a
# layer whose whole value is that its arithmetic was derived rather than ported, a
# stale one is worse than noise.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Tool output that must never reach a commit
.stellar/
mutants.out*/
fuzz/target/
fuzz/corpus/
fuzz/artifacts/

# Property-test snapshots carry no review signal, and committing them broke the
# gate that reviews the others.
#
# `proptest` seeds from entropy, so the 145 files under `test_properties/` record
# a different generated call sequence on every run. Committed, they turned
# `cargo test` into a 200 000-line diff and made CI's snapshot job fail
# unconditionally — and a gate that always fires teaches everyone to skip the
# 198 deterministic snapshots where it genuinely works.
#
# The seed is deliberately *not* pinned. Freezing it would make these files
# meaningful, at the price of turning an invariant suite that hunts for inputs
# nobody thought of into 48 fixed examples. For I1 and I5 the hunting is the
# point. The artefact worth keeping is `proptest-regressions/` — written only
# when a property actually fails, and committed, because that seed is the bug.
contracts/*/test_snapshots/test_properties/
